Changes from upstream: patterns translated to Rust regex syntax (negative
lookaheads emulated with a post-match `not_followed_by` check or code),
several patterns narrowed to reduce false positives in technical writing
(noun lists for "is the whole/entire", suffix-aligned sentence echoes,
subordinate clauses skipped for stranded auxiliaries, file names kept inside
sentences), and findings mapped onto explicit's rule and severity model.

The upstream "Signs of AI writing" pattern group (ai-vocab, not-just, not-but,
note-that, testament, crucial-role, landscape, vague-experts,
despite-challenges, participle-tail, promo, ai-leftovers) is itself adapted by
upstream from Wikipedia's "Signs of AI writing" guide
(https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Signs_of_AI_writing), licensed under
CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/). Only the ideas
behind those patterns are used here; no Wikipedia text is reproduced.

